---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Crit Value in ZZZ Explained – CV & the 1:2 Rule';
const description =
  'Crit value (CV) in Zenless Zone Zero explained: the 2×crit rate + crit damage convention, why the 1:2 ratio maximizes expected damage, and when to break it.';
const updated = SITE.lastVerified;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides' }, { name: 'Crit Value Explained' }]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Crit value explained for Zenless Zone Zero',
    datePublished: '2026-10-08',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.brand },
  }]}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Crit value explained</h1>
    <div class="h1-bar"></div>
    <p class="lede">
      One number to compare every crit stick you will ever own: CV = 2 × Crit Rate + Crit DMG. Where it comes
      from, what a good score is, and the one situation where you should ignore it.
    </p>
    <div class="microline"><span>By {SITE.brand}</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Quick answer</h2>
    <p>
      CV = 2 × Crit Rate% + Crit DMG%. A fresh endgame build sits around 100–140 CV; strong builds reach
      160–200+ [community conventions]. It works because crit rate is roughly twice as scarce as crit damage on
      disc rolls — double-weighting it makes CV a fair one-number comparison. Check yours in the{' '}
      <a href="/crit-ratio/">crit ratio analyzer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Why the 1:2 ratio wins</h2>
    <p>Expected damage multiplies by (1 + CR × CD). With a fixed "crit budget" to spend on the two stats, the product CR × CD is maximized when CD = 2 × CR:</p>
    <pre class="formula">budget 180 units → 60/120: 1 + 0.60×1.20 = ×1.72
                 → 45/90 : ×1.41  (too little of both)
                 → 75/150: ×2.13  (needs more budget — richer build)</pre>
    <p>Same budget, different split, very different multiplier. That's why two builds with identical CV can still differ — CV ranks your gear; the <em>ratio</em> decides how much of it converts to damage.</p>

    <h2>When to break the rule</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Below ~50% crit rate:</strong> rotations become coin-flippy; push rate even past the ratio for consistency.</li>
      <li><strong>Buffs that grant crit:</strong> if your team or W-Engine adds crit rate, rebalance toward CD.</li>
      <li><strong>Big one-sided upgrades:</strong> a disc with +14% CD and no rate is still an upgrade — take it, rebalance later. Verify with the <a href="/damage-calculator/">damage calculator</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Related tools</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/crit-ratio/">Crit Ratio Analyzer</a> — compare two builds' expected multipliers head-to-head.</li>
      <li><a href="/disc-scorer/">Disc Scorer</a> — CV per disc, plus roll value for non-crit builds.</li>
      <li><a href="/damage-calculator/">Damage Calculator</a> — turn crit stats into actual hit numbers.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
